      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto, main text",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>\n<p>In the name of God, the merciful, the compassionate. Trust [in God] [?].</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>In the law court at the Musallamiyya madrasa in the port of Damietta the well-protected, before our master, the poor slave in need of God the exalted, the shaykh, the most evident imam,</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>the knowledgeable, the erudite, the ornament of religion, the glory of the \u02bfulama\u0304\u02be, unique among the favoured, the indisputable mufti, Abi\u0304 Hurayra \u02bfAbd al-Rah\u0323man</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>al-Ak\u0323s\u0323ara\u0304yi\u0304 the H\u0323anbali\u0304, the great deputy judge in the aforementioned port, may God the exalted support his judgements and favour him with probity.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The two full brothers Abu\u0304 al-Baqa\u0304\u02be and Abu\u0304 al-\u02bfIzz, sons of the late Badr al-Di\u0304n, [also] known as Budayr, son of the late al-Shiha\u0304bi\u0304</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ah\u0323mad, [also] known as Bi\u0304ghos (Bey) al-H\u0323arami\u0304, their grandfather, in Ghayd al-Nas\u0323a\u0304ra in the aforementioned port, and Mu\u02bfallim Joseph the son of Mu\u02bfallim Abraham Castro,</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>the current \u02bfa\u0304mil of the aforementioned port, who is trusted by the two of them, reached a legal agreement while in a state of health, well-being, free will, and choice, that that to which</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>the aforementioned Mu\u02bfallim Joseph is entitled&mdash;that is owed by Abi\u0304 al-Baqa\u0304\u02be and Abi\u0304 al-\u02bfIzz, mentioned above, of [?]...the legal tax farm</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>to their aforementioned father Budayr, or to their aforementioned grandfather Ah\u0323mad Bi\u0304ghos, of legal debts prior to this date and from enterprises among them&mdash;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>totals, in large Ottoman silver coins current in Egypt now, 1000 nis\u0323f [fid\u0323d\u0323a] and 500 nis\u0323f legal liability,</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>by legal means, by way of exigible debt. Abu\u0304 al-Baqa\u0304\u02be and Abu\u0304 al-\u02bfIzz, mentioned above, and they are the first party in what is to be mentioned,</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>and the aforementioned Mu\u02bfallim Joseph, and he is by himself the second party to the legal settlement, acknowledged in a legal acknowledgement that neither party</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>is entitled to [anything] or has any right to [anything] from the other after this. The aforementioned Mu\u02bfallim Joseph added to his acknowledgement that he was not</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>entitled, on his own behalf or that of his father the aforementioned Abraham, [to anything more] from the first party or from the debt of the aforementioned Budayr or the debt of his father</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ah\u0323mad Bi\u0304ghos or any of their heirs, [no] right, no entitlement, no claim, no demand in any manner or [for any] reason,</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>not in silver, gold, or copper, not by seizure or confiscation, not by account or by an error in one, not in ignorance or</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>forgetfulness or absentmindedness, not through debt or in cash, not by testament, not by borrowing, not through coercion, no claim to this,</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>nothing at all, a little or much, great or humble, blameworthy or trustworthy, directly or through an agent [?], fixed</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>or mobile, of whatever type or kind or description, not in valuables and not by liability, not by swearing</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>by God the exalted, nothing, not a little nor much, from previous times to the present day, except for what was owed to the aforementioned Joseph by Abi\u0304 al-Baqa\u0304\u02be</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>and Abi\u0304 al-\u02bfIzz, mentioned above, and that is the amount agreed to above and the items of pledge that will be enumerated on the right of the verso,</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>which he pledged today to his heirs on that basis. Each party released the debt, hand, and pledge of the other</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>for all the valuables, liabilities, claims, demands, and obligatory oaths&mdash;a legal, definitive, firm, final release,</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>...overriding all rights, claims, and oaths before this date and until this date, except for those named above. Each of the two parties accepted.</p>\n</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
